        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Context Indetifying LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767352172985"
          },
          "code": "CONTEXT_INDETIFYING_LLM",
          "id": "1775645107467",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775645107469_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict information extraction engine. Your task is to extract structured data from a user query and return a JSON object in EXACTLY the following format:\nINPUT QUERY:\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n{\n\"context\": \"NOTHING | ITEM | POINT_OF_USE | KANBAN_CARD | UNMOVED_CARD\",\n\"items\": [],\n\"point_of_use\": {\n\"subinventory\": [],\n\"locator\": [],\n\"lpn\": []\n},\n\"kanban_card\": [],\n\"days\": [],\n\"thresholdPercent\": []\n}\n\nIMPORTANT RULES (MUST FOLLOW STRICTLY):\n\n1. OUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n* Return ONLY valid JSON.\n* Do NOT include explanations, comments, or extra text.\n* Do NOT change key names or structure.\n* All arrays must always be present, even if empty.\n\n2. CONTEXT PRIORITY (VERY IMPORTANT):\n   Determine ONLY ONE context using this strict priority order:\n   ITEM > POINT_OF_USE > KANBAN_CARD > UNMOVED_CARD > NOTHING\n\n3. ITEM DETECTION:\n   If the query mentions item(s), SKU(s), product(s), or material(s), extract all identifiers.\n   Examples:\n\n* \"item ABC123\"\n* \"items ABC123, XYZ456\"\n  Set:\n* context = \"ITEM\"\n* items = list of extracted values\n\n4. POINT_OF_USE DETECTION:\n   If subinventory, locator, or LPN is mentioned:\n\n* context = \"POINT_OF_USE\"\n* Extract values into:\n\n  * subinventory\n  * locator\n  * lpn\n    Each should be a list.\n\n5. KANBAN CARD DETECTION:\n   If \"kanban card\" or \"card\" followed by an identifier is mentioned:\n\n* context = \"KANBAN_CARD\"\n* Extract all card numbers\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n* Ignore phrases like \"card status\", \"card type\"\n* Ignore \"unmoved card\" in this step\n\n6. UNMOVED CARD DETECTION:\n   If the query mentions \"unmoved card\" and a number of days:\n   Example:\n\n* \"unmoved card for 3 days\"\n  Set:\n* context = \"UNMOVED_CARD\"\n* days = [number as string]\n\n7.DAYS EXTRACTION (NEW - APPLIES TO ALL CONTEXTS):\n\nExtract numeric values representing a time duration in days whenever mentioned.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"past 90 days\" → [\"90\"]\n\"last 7 days\" → [\"7\"]\n\"for 30 days\" → [\"30\"]\n\nRules:\n\nCapture only when clearly referring to a duration in days\nStore values as strings\nDo NOT infer or convert from weeks/months\nThis applies even if context is ITEM, POINT_OF_USE, or KANBAN_CARD\n\n8. THRESHOLD EXTRACTION (NEW - APPLIES TO ALL CONTEXTS):\n\nExtract numeric values representing threshold percentage whenever explicitly mentioned.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"over 5%\" → [\"5\"]\n\"threshold 3 percent\" → [\"3\"]\n\"more than 4% of lead time\" → [\"4\"]\n\nRules:\n\nCapture only explicit percentage thresholds\nStore values as strings without the % sign\nDo NOT infer default values\nDo NOT convert from words (e.g., \"five percent\")\nThis applies even if context is ITEM, POINT_OF_USE, KANBAN_CARD, or UNMOVED_CARD\n\n9. NOTHING CASE:\n   If none of the above apply:\n\n* context = \"NOTHING\"\n* All arrays must be empty\n\n10. CLEAN EXTRACTION RULES:\n\n* Split multiple values by comma or space\n* Trim whitespace\n* Do NOT invent values\n* Do NOT infer missing data\n\n11. STRICTNESS:\n\n* If multiple contexts appear, ALWAYS choose based on priority\n* Never return multiple contexts\n* Never mix contexts\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn ONLY the JSON object.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
